1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:02,300
Hi, I'm Jason Siever.

2
00:00:03,260 --> 00:00:04,020
I'm a psychiatrist.

3
00:00:04,360 --> 00:00:07,120
I've spent the last 15 years helping people with their problems.

4
00:00:07,320 --> 00:00:08,520
And I'm Maggie Siever.

5
00:00:08,840 --> 00:00:12,640
I've spent the last 15 years helping our kids with problems even Jason wouldn't

6
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:16,800
believe. Now Maggie has gone back to work as a reporter for the local newspaper.

7
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:20,400
And Jason has moved his practice into the house so he can be there for the kids.

8
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:21,380
They're great kids.

9
00:00:21,540 --> 00:00:22,580
Most of the time.

10
00:00:22,680 --> 00:00:23,940
And the rest of the time?

11
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:26,060
We love them anyway.

12
00:00:26,380 --> 00:00:28,240
Yeah. Unbelievable.

13
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:34,060
Show me that smile again.

14
00:00:35,140 --> 00:00:38,700
Don't waste another minute on your crying.

15
00:00:39,060 --> 00:00:41,920
We're nowhere near the end.

16
00:00:42,180 --> 00:00:46,220
The fest is ready to begin.

17
00:00:46,840 --> 00:00:48,640
Oh, oh, oh, oh.

18
00:00:48,640 --> 00:00:55,160
As long as we got each other, we got the world spinning right.

19
00:00:55,240 --> 00:00:59,900
And our hands, baby, you and me, we got to be.

20
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:09,260
The luckiest dreamers who never quit dreaming As long as we keep on giving We can

21
00:01:09,260 --> 00:01:18,480
take anything that comes our way Baby rain or shine all the time We got each other

22
00:01:18,480 --> 00:01:20,380
sharing the laughter

23
00:01:38,900 --> 00:01:40,060
Here we go.

24
00:01:40,240 --> 00:01:42,140
How many for scrambled eggs?

25
00:01:47,840 --> 00:01:49,900
Okay, how many for last night's liver?

26
00:01:52,020 --> 00:01:53,680
Now how many for scrambled eggs?

27
00:01:53,680 --> 00:01:55,120
Uh -huh. Uh -huh.

28
00:01:56,440 --> 00:01:59,880
Dad, I'm having some trouble with my science project.

29
00:02:00,100 --> 00:02:01,560
Uh -huh. You need some help with it?

30
00:02:01,560 --> 00:02:02,920
I need to know what it is.

31
00:02:05,880 --> 00:02:08,140
Well, uh, what are you studying in science?

32
00:02:08,580 --> 00:02:11,500
Science stuff. Okay.

33
00:02:11,680 --> 00:02:12,660
That's a good start.

34
